{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '430,492p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.cursor-cell-numbering.md; sed -n '720,810p' collab/numbering-probe/src/probe/discovery.clj; git status --short; git diff --stat\"","aggregated_output":"disjoint and each `Uᵢ` is confined to `Cᵢ` (every occurrence of an\nunnumbered cell lies in a tied element, hence in its own component).\nEqual, complete encodings of `[:component g₁ i₁ …]` rows are a faithful\nspelling (literals as themselves, rows expanded, every cursor cell by\nindex and body rank, groups by sequence number, a group's several\nelements as a sorted set), so they exhibit, for each pair `Cᵢ, Cⱼ`, a\nbijection `Uᵢ → Uⱼ` under which the components are the same structure\ngroup by group. Entering the run in host order `σ` gives the cells of\n`C_{σ(t)}` the numbers `b + (t−1)·|U| + 1 …` by local index; in order\n`σ'` the cells of `C_{σ'(t)}` receive the same numbers. The block-swap\nbijection composed from the pairwise bijections is an isomorphism of the\ntwo resulting configurations: numbers agree by construction, structures\nagree because the swapped components are isomorphic and nothing outside\nthem mentions their cells, and the worklists agree because the same\ngroups remain, with the same elements removed. ∎\n\n**Lemma D (the D5 verdict is invariant).** Whether the root run, or a\ncomponent run it requires, reaches a fixpoint with a conflicting\ncomponent depends only on which tied elements share unnumbered cursor\ncells at that fixpoint, which is a function of the configuration up to\nisomorphism (lemma A gives the ties, the sharing relation is structural);\nand whether a component run is complete is the same question one level\ndown, by the induction. Key runs do not enter the verdict: their\nconflicts are spelled, not refused, and the spelling is canonical (lemma\nA iii).\n\n**Lemma E (D6 trials).** At a conflicting component the set `E` of\nelements of its least conflicting group is a function of the\nconfiguration up to isomorphism (lemma D names the component and its\ngroups canonically). Each trial is a deterministic function of (the\nconfiguration up to isomorphism, the chosen element), by the induction\non the trial run, which has strictly fewer unnumbered cells than the\nenclosing run (its forced element holds at least one, being linked into\nthe component by a shared unnumbered cell). So the multiset of trial\nspellings is canonical and its least member is canonical. Two trials\nwith equal least spellings have produced isomorphic numberings of the\ncomponent (faithful spelling, as in lemma C), so adopting either yields\nisomorphic configurations. ∎\n\n**Theorem.** The procedure's output on isomorphic configurations is the\nsame: both refuse at corresponding points, or both emit byte-identical\nrows. *Proof.* By the induction above. D1 and D2 decisions are functions\nof the configuration up to isomorphism (lemma A); D3 only repeats D1 on\ndeferred groups in a canonical order; D4's choice of the least run is\ncanonical (lemma A on component encodings, which are complete by D5/D6)\nand its only listed-order input is harmless (lemma C); D5 is invariant\n(lemma D); D6 is invariant (lemma E). Emission spells cursor cells by\nnumber only and sorts every emitted unordered slot by canonical bytes\nunder the final numbering (carrier §5), so isomorphic final\nconfigurations emit the same rows. ∎\n\nConsequences:\n\n1. *Function of structure, renaming-invariant, enumeration-invariant*:\n   the theorem with `π` a renaming, a permutation of the containers, or\n   both. No decision reads a source id or a host order except at the\n   point lemma C covers.\n2. *Terminating.* The structural edge family is acyclic (carrier §8 step\n   3), so every traversal is finite. In any run each D3 round that is not\n   the last numbers a cursor cell; each D4 step numbers at least one\n   cursor cell or removes a duplicate group; each local run is over an\n   item with fewer unordered containers nested below it than its\n   spawning run's item, or (a trial) with fewer unnumbered cells, so the\n  \"`parent` with one install 'a holding `child` (slot 3 set to :child).\"\n  [parent child]\n  (rows/node :task (assoc (:slots parent) 12\n                          [(rows/node :install ['a :running nil {} (rows/node :task (assoc (:slots child) 3 :child))])])))\n\n;; ------------------------------------------------------------ diagnostics\n\n(defn permissive-roots\n  \"For a refused state: run the procedure with D5 replaced by host-first entry,\n   over `n` shuffles of every unordered container. More than one root is a\n   witness that the state is not interchangeable; one root over n shuffles is\n   not a proof.\"\n  [task n]\n  (let [r (java.util.Random. 7)]\n    (with-redefs [shuffle (seeded-shuffle r)]\n      (->> (repeatedly n #(rename-and-shuffle task identity))\n           (map (fn [t] (binding [*numbering-opts* (assoc *numbering-opts* :permissive true)]\n                          (let [d (discovery-numbering t)\n                                [id _] (emit-node* t (:numbering d) {} [])]\n                            id))))\n           distinct count))))\n\n(defn invariant-roots\n  \"Distinct roots of a state over `n` renamings plus shuffles (1 = invariant\n   under the samples).\"\n  [task n]\n  (let [r (java.util.Random. 5) cells (all-census-cells task)]\n    (with-redefs [shuffle (seeded-shuffle r)]\n      (->> (repeatedly n #(rename-and-shuffle task (zipmap cells (map (fn [i] (keyword \"r\" (str \"z\" i))) (shuffle (range (count cells)))))))\n           (map do-root)\n           distinct count))))\n\n(defn report-fixture [name task]\n  (let [d (discovery-numbering task)]\n    (println name)\n    (println \"  DO :\" (or (:refused d) (into (sorted-map) (:numbering d))) \"| work\" (:work (:used d)) \"| search\" (or (:search (:used d)) 0))\n    (println \"  DO root:\" (do-root task))\n    (println \"  6a root:\" (safe-6a-root task))))\n\n(defn invariance-check\n  \"Root of the state and of the state renamed and shuffled; decode of the\n   carrier. Returns a map of outcomes.\"\n  [task ^java.util.Random r]\n  (let [cells (all-census-cells task)\n        fresh (zipmap cells (map #(keyword \"other\" (str \"z\" %)) (shuffle (range (count cells)))))\n        task2 (with-redefs [shuffle (seeded-shuffle r)] (rename-and-shuffle task fresh))\n        d1 (do-root task) d2 (do-root task2)]\n    (cond\n      (and (map? d1) (:refused d1)) {:refused (:refused d1)}\n      (map? d1) {:resource-limit (:resource-limit d1)}\n      :else\n      (cond-> {:root d1 :invariant (= d1 d2)\n               :used (:used (discovery-numbering task))}\n        true (assoc :decode (let [e (error #(decode* (emit* task)))]\n                              (cond (nil? e) :ok\n                                    (= :resource-limit (:yin.k/kind e)) :sixa-recompute-limit\n                                    :else e)))))))\n\n(defn search [label gen seeds]\n  (let [r (java.util.Random. 11)\n        stats (atom {:numbered 0 :refused 0 :resource-limit 0 :invariance-fail 0 :decode-ok 0 :decode-fail 0 :decode-6a-limit 0\n                     :refused-witnessed-noninterchangeable 0 :refused-not-distinguished 0\n                     :max-work 0 :max-search 0 :max-local-runs 0})]\n    (doseq [seed seeds]\n      (let [task (gen seed) o (invariance-check task r)]\n        (cond\n          (:refused o)\n          (do (swap! stats update :refused inc)\n              (if (> (permissive-roots task 12) 1)\n                (swap! stats update :refused-witnessed-noninterchangeable inc)\n                (swap! stats update :refused-not-distinguished inc)))\n          (:resource-limit o)\n          (do (swap! stats update :resource-limit inc) (println \"RESOURCE LIMIT\" label seed (:resource-limit o)))\n          :else\n          (do (swap! stats update :numbered inc)\n              (swap! stats update :max-work max (:work (:used o) 0))\n              (swap! stats update :max-search max (:search (:used o) 0))\n              (swap! stats update :max-local-runs max (:local-runs (:used o) 0))\n              (when-not (:invariant o) (swap! stats update :invariance-fail inc) (println \"INVARIANCE FAIL\" label seed))\n              (case (:decode o)\n                :ok (swap! stats update :decode-ok inc)\n                :sixa-recompute-limit (swap! stats update :decode-6a-limit inc)\n                (do (swap! stats update :decode-fail inc) (println \"DECODE FAIL\" label seed (:decode o))))))))\n    (println label (count seeds) \"states:\" @stats)\n    @stats))\n\n(defn -main []\n  (let [body (rt/cursor-cell-body :s 0)\n        s (fn [es] [:row (rows/node :set es)])\n        v (fn [cs] [:row (rows/node :vec (mapv #(vector :cursor-cell %) cs))])\n        c (fn [x] [:cursor-cell x])\n M docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.cursor-cell-numbering.md\n?? collab/1792120000000-architect-cursor-cell-numbering.claude-fable-5-1.stdout.log\n?? collab/1792120000000-architect-cursor-cell-numbering.prompt.md\n?? collab/1792120000000-architect-cursor-cell-numbering.report.md\n?? collab/1792140000000-architect-cursor-cell-numbering-review.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md\n?? collab/1792140000000-architect-cursor-cell-numbering-review.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\n?? collab/1792140000000-architect-cursor-cell-numbering-review.prompt.md\n?? collab/1792150000000-architect-cursor-cell-numbering-revise.claude-fable-5-1.stdout.log\n?? collab/1792150000000-architect-cursor-cell-numbering-revise.prompt.md\n?? collab/1792150000000-architect-cursor-cell-numbering-revise.report.md\n?? collab/1792170000000-architect-cursor-cell-numbering-review-r2.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md\n?? collab/1792170000000-architect-cursor-cell-numbering-review-r2.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\n?? collab/1792170000000-architect-cursor-cell-numbering-review-r2.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout2.log\n?? collab/1792170000000-architect-cursor-cell-numbering-review-