{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '215,242p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.cursor-cell-numbering.md; rg -n 'defn.*bytes-key|defn.*byte-compare' collab/numbering-probe/src/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; git show srvm-phase6a:src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc | shasum; shasum collab/numbering-probe/src/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; git show srvm-phase6a:test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc | shasum; shasum collab/numbering-probe/src/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '215,242p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.cursor-cell-numbering.md; rg -n 'defn.*bytes-key|defn.*byte-compare' collab/numbering-probe/src/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; git show srvm-phase6a:src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc | shasum; shasum collab/numbering-probe/src/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; git show srvm-phase6a:test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc | shasum; shasum collab/numbering-probe/src/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"## 2. The rule (replaces carrier §6 \"The procedure\")\n\nInput: the abstract task of carrier §6 (the §5 structure with cursor\ncells as identities, before numbering). Output: a bijection from the\ntask's reached cursor cells to `:yin.k/cc-1 … :yin.k/cc-n`, or a\nrefusal. Install children are numbered as their own tasks by the same\nrule (task boundary, unchanged), in any order, since scopes are disjoint.\n\n**Spelling (the content encoding `CE`).** A run spells the item it has\ntraversed under its final numbering. The root run spells a cursor cell\nnumbered `k` as `[:cursor-cell [:n k]]`, `k` an exact integer; a local\nrun spells a cursor cell it numbered itself (index `j`, counted from the\nenclosing run's local counter) as `[:cursor-cell [:u j r]]`, `r` the\ncell's body rank (an exact integer; rank order equals body-label order,\nso no comparison and no numbering changes against spelling the label,\nand the key's size no longer depends on the descriptor), and a cursor\ncell numbered by an enclosing run as that run spelled it. Nothing else\nchanges from carrier §6 step 2: `[:lit d]` as itself, `[:row B]`\nexpanded in place, structural data as itself, the census as\n`[:cursor-cells]`, an install child as `[:child]` (replacing step 2's\n`[:child <child root id>]`: a child sits only under a name-keyed install\nentry, never inside an unordered container, so its content never decides\nan order, and the encoding stays hash-free). Keyed structural rows are\nspelled in their canonical key order, `:window` in numeric register\norder; a `:set` or `:map` is spelled as the bytewise sorted vector of its\nelements' spellings (an entry as `[:entry K V]`), duplicates retained,\nwhere a tie group the run could not resolve is spelled in place as\n`[:tie K … K]` (its common key, once per element). All comparisons are\n91:(defn- bytes-key\n107:(defn- byte-compare\ne02350337c1b48a8d02901e46499d4cd0ab90f19  -\ne02350337c1b48a8d02901e46499d4cd0ab90f19  collab/numbering-probe/src/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc\nd8aeed70b39a1f4770ba99fb699d06e6561a4128  -\nd8aeed70b39a1f4770ba99fb699d06e6561a4128  collab/numbering-probe/src/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"mise exec -- java -Xmx1g @java.args clojure.main - <<'CLJ'\n(require '[probe.discovery :as p] '[yin.vm.ucf.rows :as r] '[yin.vm.ucf.rows-test :as t])\n(def rng (java.util.Random. 179221))\n(defn sh [xs] (let [a (java.util.ArrayList. (vec xs))] (java.util.Collections/shuffle a rng) (vec a)))\n(defn c [x] [:cursor-cell x])\n(defn v [xs] [:row (r/node :vec (vec xs))])\n(defn s [xs] [:row (r/node :set (vec (distinct xs)))])\n(defn m [ps] [:row (r/node :map (vec (mapcat identity ps)))])\n(def b (t/cursor-cell-body :s 0))\n(defn task [value] (t/task-node (mapv #(vector % b) (sort (p/reached value))) value))\n(defn rename2 [n bij]\n (letfn [(val2 [x] (case (first x) :cursor-cell (c (bij (second x))) :row [:row (go (second x))] x))\n         (go [n] (let [ss (:slots n) k (:kind n)]\n          (r/node k (case k\n           :set (sh (mapv val2 ss))\n           :map (vec (mapcat identity (sh (mapv (fn [[a z]] [(val2 a) (val2 z)]) (partition 2 ss)))))\n           :cursor-cells (vec (mapcat identity (sh (mapv (fn [[a z]] [(bij a) (go z)]) (partition 2 ss)))))\n           (mapv (fn [d x] (cond (p/ref? d) (go x) (p/refs? d) (mapv go x) (= :C d) (bij x) (p/v? d) (when x (val2 x)) :else x)) (p/descriptors k ss) ss)))))] (go n)))\n(defn gen [i]\n (let [n (+ 2 (.nextInt rng 7)) cs (vec (range n)) cc #(c (nth cs (.nextInt rng n)))\n       edge #(v [(cc) (cc)]) es (vec (repeatedly (+ 2 (.nextInt rng 9)) edge))\n       group #(s (repeatedly (+ 2 (.nextInt rng 4)) cc))\n       value (case (mod i 10)\n         0 (s es)\n         1 (v [(s es) (s (sh es))])\n         2 (s (repeatedly 4 group))\n         3 (v [(s es) (cc)])\n         4 (s (map #(v [% (group)]) es))\n         5 (m (mapv (fn [x] [(c x) (cc)]) cs))\n         6 (v [(s es) (s (map #(v (reverse (:slots (second %)))) es))])\n         7 (s (map #(m [[(cc) %] [[:lit :anchor] (group)]]) es))\n         8 (s [(v [(s es) (group)]) (v [(group) (s (sh es))])])\n         9 (v [(s es) (s (repeatedly 4 group)) (cc)]))\n       root (task value)]\n  (if (zero? (mod i 20)) (p/with-child (t/task-node [] [:lit nil]) root) root)))\n(def stats (atom {}))\n(defn norm [x] (if (keyword? x) x (if (:refused x) :refused x)))\n(doseq [i (range 5000)]\n (let [q (gen i) ids (p/all-census-cells q)\n       copies (vec (repeatedly 2 #(rename2 q (zipmap ids (sh (mapv (fn [j] (keyword \\\"fresh\\\" (str j))) (range (count ids))))))))]\n  (doseq [mode [false true]]\n   (binding [p/*numbering-opts* {:residue-search mode}]\n    (let [outcomes (mapv p/do-root (cons q copies))]\n     (swap\"'! stats update [mode (if (keyword? (first outcomes)) :numbered (norm (first outcomes)))] (fnil inc 0))\n     (when-not (apply = (map norm outcomes)) (println \"MISMATCH\" i mode (pr-str q) outcomes) (throw (ex-info \"mismatch\" {})))\n     (when (and (< i 100) (keyword? (first outcomes)))\n       (let [e (p/error #(p/decode* (p/emit* q)))]\n        (swap! stats update [mode :decode (if (nil? e) :ok (:yin.k/kind e))] (fnil inc 0))))))))\n (when (zero? (mod (inc i) 1000)) (println \"PROGRESS\" (inc i))))\n(println \"COUNTS\" @stats)\nCLJ'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"Two targeted tests contradict F4’s coverage claims: D5 can refuse a component with mixed body labels, and an ordered reference to one cell need not resolve the whole component. Budget accounting also remains incomplete: a nested fixture creates 1,574 encoded key bytes while charging 77 work units, and the prototype accepts 20,000 cells despite the default 64-cell limit."}}
