{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.cursor-cell-numbering.md | sed -n '484,497p;767,793p;884,900p'; nl -ba collab/numbering-probe/src/probe/discovery.clj | sed -n '254,278p;325,340p;370,406p'; sed -n '530,575p' collab/numbering-probe/src/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"   484\t   the theorem with `π` a renaming, a permutation of the containers, or\n   485\t   both. No decision reads a source id or a host order except at the\n   486\t   point lemma C covers.\n   487\t2. *Terminating.* The structural edge family is acyclic (carrier §8 step\n   488\t   3), so every traversal is finite. In any run each D3 round that is not\n   489\t   the last numbers a cursor cell; each D4 step numbers at least one\n   490\t   cursor cell or removes a duplicate group; each local run is over an\n   491\t   item with fewer unordered containers nested below it than its\n   492\t   spawning run's item, or (a trial) with fewer unnumbered cells, so the\n   493\t   induction measure of §3 decreases and there are finitely many local\n   494\t   runs. The budget of §2 \"Work\" is what bounds the count.\n   495\t3. *Deterministic*, hence two lifts of one state are byte-identical and\n   496\t   the receiver's recomputation is well defined.\n   497\t4. *Sharing survives*: the numbering is a bijection on reached cursor\n   767\t**Adopt discovery order with D6** (owner decision: adopt; D6 is this\n   768\tnote's recommendation within it). 6b has not started and 6a is\n   769\tunmerged, so the cost is one implementation slice of `rows.cljc` and its\n   770\ttests (§8) plus the amendments of §4. Size, from the prototype and the\n   771\tsecond review's count rather than the round-2 guess: the prototype's\n   772\tschema-to-procedure region is about 330 nonblank lines, of which about\n   773\t30 are D6, the diagnostic mode, tracing and measurement; in place it\n   774\treuses 6a