` and cells `[A B]`.\n   891\t- `intermediate-label-bytes-are-bounded` (`:400-403`) →\n   892\t  `seven-cursor-cells-number-by-residue-search` (D6: root `d76d787a…`,\n   893\t  11 trials, `{:search 10}` → `:resource-limit [:search]`) or, in the D5\n   894\t  variant, `seven-cursor-cells-are-refused` (`:unresolved-cursor-cells`,\n   895\t  cells `[a b c d e f g]`).\n   896\t- `input-row-bodies-do-not-spend-label-bytes` (`:406-421`) →\n   897\t  `large-literals-do-not-spend-work-beyond-their-bytes`, same body: a\n   898\t  400000-element literal still emits and decodes under the default\n   899\t  budget.\n   900\t\n   254\t                                  [:row {:kind :set :slots (mapv #(elem-item (:kind %) (:elem %)) ms)}])])\n   255\t                             (partition-by :group (:members comp))))}])\n   256\t\n   257\t(defn- component-encoding\n   258\t  \"D4 for a certified component: a local run over its item, required to be\n   259\t   complete. D5 for a conflicting component: refuse. D6 (:residue-search): one\n   260\t   trial per element of the duplicated group, that element entered first; the\n   261\t   least complete spelling is the encoding. :permissive (diagnostic only):\n   262\t   a single trial with the host-first element.\"\n   263\t  [run comp]\n   264\t  (let [ctx (:ctx run) item (component-item comp)]\n   265\t    (cond\n   266\t      (not (:conflict comp)) (local-run run item nil)\n   267\t      (:permissive ctx)\n   268\t      (let [m (first (filter #(= (:dup-group comp) (:group %)) (:members comp)))]\n   269\t        (local-run run item (elem-item (:kind m) (:elem m))))\n   270\t      (:residue-search ctx)\n   271\t      (let [es (filter #(= (:dup-group comp) (:group %)) (:members comp))\n   272\t            trials (mapv (fn [m] (spend! ctx :search 1) (local-run run item (elem-item (:kind m) (:elem m)))) es)]\n   273\t        (when (and *trace* (= :n (:tag run)))\n   274\t          (doseq [t trials] (println \"  [trial]\" (:complete? t) (: